1
00:00:07,830 --> 00:00:11,960
A concert ticket went up from 60 dollars to 75 dollars.

2
00:00:12,010 --> 00:00:15,770
The organiser says it is only a small rise.

3
00:00:15,820 --> 00:00:18,380
By what percentage did the price rise?

4
00:00:18,430 --> 00:00:21,970
Pause the video and work it out.

5
00:00:22,020 --> 00:00:23,890
The rise is 15 dollars.

6
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:27,820
Compare it with the original price, 60 dollars.

7
00:00:27,870 --> 00:00:31,660
15 divided by 60 is 0.25, which is 25 percent.

8
00:00:31,710 --> 00:00:35,300
That is a quarter more, not so small!

9
00:00:35,350 --> 00:00:40,830
Remember: to find 15 percent of 80, multiply 0.15 by 80.

10
00:00:40,880 --> 00:00:42,470
That is 12.

11
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:47,310
To increase an amount by a percentage, find the percentage, then add it.

12
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:50,480
To decrease, find it, then subtract it.

13
00:00:50,530 --> 00:00:51,330
Your turn.

14
00:00:51,380 --> 00:00:53,610
Increase 200 by 35 percent.

15
00:00:53,660 --> 00:00:57,290
Pause the video and try it.

16
00:00:57,340 --> 00:01:00,530
35 percent of 200 is 70.

17
00:01:00,580 --> 00:01:03,650
200 plus 70 is 270.

18
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:09,530
The percentage change is the change, divided by the original amount, times 100.

19
00:01:09,580 --> 00:01:12,840
Always divide by the original amount.

20
00:01:12,890 --> 00:01:16,870
The actual change, 15 dollars, is the absolute change.

21
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:19,400
25 percent is the relative change.

22
00:01:19,450 --> 00:01:24,650
Percentages make it fair to compare changes of different sizes.

23
00:01:24,700 --> 00:01:25,970
Here is the method.

24
00:01:26,020 --> 00:01:33,020
Step 1: to increase or decrease, find the percentage of the original, then add or subtract it.

25
00:01:33,070 --> 00:01:39,340
Step 2: for a percentage change, find the change: the new amount minus the original.

26
00:01:39,390 --> 00:01:44,230
Step 3: divide by the original, and multiply by 100.

27
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:48,440
Step 4: say whether it is an increase or a decrease.

28
00:01:48,490 --> 00:01:51,340
A laptop costs 850 dollars.

29
00:01:51,390 --> 00:01:54,350
It is reduced by 12 percent.

30
00:01:54,400 --> 00:01:57,030
12 percent of 850 is 102.

31
00:01:57,080 --> 00:02:00,690
850 minus 102 is 748 dollars.

32
00:02:00,740 --> 00:02:01,450
Your turn.

33
00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:04,800
A price falls from 80 dollars to 68 dollars.

34
00:02:04,850 --> 00:02:07,230
What is the percentage decrease?

35
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:10,300
Pause and work it out.

36
00:02:10,350 --> 00:02:12,700
The change is 12 dollars.

37
00:02:12,750 --> 00:02:16,060
12 divided by 80, times 100, is 15.

38
00:02:16,110 --> 00:02:19,300
It is a 15 percent decrease.

39
00:02:19,350 --> 00:02:23,120
In shop A, a price went from 40 to 46 dollars.

40
00:02:23,170 --> 00:02:26,020
In shop B, from 120 to 132 dollars.

41
00:02:26,070 --> 00:02:29,650
Which had the bigger percentage rise?

42
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:32,730
Shop A: 6 divided by 40 is 15 percent.

43
00:02:32,780 --> 00:02:35,980
Shop B: 12 divided by 120 is 10 percent.

44
00:02:36,030 --> 00:02:42,940
Shop A had the bigger percentage rise, even though shop B rose more in dollars.

45
00:02:42,990 --> 00:02:46,320
A price falls from 50 dollars to 40 dollars.

46
00:02:46,370 --> 00:02:48,930
Jay finds the percentage decrease.

47
00:02:48,980 --> 00:02:51,630
Which line goes wrong first?

48
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:52,820
Line 2 is wrong.

49
00:02:52,870 --> 00:02:54,900
He divided by the new price.

50
00:02:54,950 --> 00:02:58,580
You must divide by the original price, 50.

51
00:02:58,630 --> 00:03:03,860
10 divided by 50, times 100, is 20 percent.

52
00:03:03,910 --> 00:03:08,590
Governments track population changes as percentages.

53
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:12,870
A town fell from 25,000 people to 23,500.

54
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:14,710
The change is 1,500.

55
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:18,480
1,500 divided by 25,000, times 100, is 6.

56
00:03:18,530 --> 00:03:26,290
That is a 6 percent decrease, which helps compare it with towns of other sizes.

57
00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:27,750
One last question.

58
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:29,860
Decrease 90 by 10 percent.

59
00:03:29,910 --> 00:03:33,450
Pause the video and answer.

60
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:36,030
10 percent of 90 is 9.

61
00:03:36,080 --> 00:03:38,580
90 minus 9 is 81.

62
00:03:38,630 --> 00:03:41,700
To remember: to increase, add the percentage.

63
00:03:41,750 --> 00:03:43,990
To decrease, subtract it.

64
00:03:44,040 --> 00:03:50,080
Percentage change equals the change, divided by the original, times 100.

65
00:03:50,130 --> 00:03:55,300
Know the difference between absolute change and percentage change.

66
00:03:55,350 --> 00:03:58,820
Use percentages to compare changes fairly.

67
00:03:58,870 --> 00:04:04,230
Great work! Now practise lesson 10.1 on Camday.
